# Naga Fleshcrafter: "Renew — {2}{U}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Put a +1/+1 counter on target nonlegendary creature
# you control. Each other creature you control becomes a copy of that creature until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery."
# On turn 1 Bot1 casts Memnite, Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer and a Naga Fleshcrafter it declines to have copy, so it dies. On
# Bot2's turn 2 a Phyrexian Walker comes down. On turn 3 the ability refuses the legendary Ragavan as its target
# (CR 205.4a) and Bot2's nonlegendary Walker, a creature Bot1 doesn't control; aimed at Memnite it exiles the Naga, puts a
# +1/+1 counter on Memnite (2/2) and makes Ragavan, the one other creature Bot1 controls, a Memnite (a 1/1 artifact
# Construct, never legendary) until end of turn - while Bot2's Phyrexian Walker is still a Walker (CR 611.2c, 707.2). As the turn passes to Bot2's turn 4 Ragavan is the 2/1 Monkey Pirate again
# (CR 514.2) and Memnite keeps its counter.

